### Learning lab: TheHive 5 REST calls used by the Shuffle workflows (VS Code "REST Client" format).

@thehive = http://<thehive-host>:9000
@apiKey = <thehive-api-key-never-commit>

### 1. Create a case
# @name case
POST {{thehive}}/api/v1/case
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Brute force then success for lab.victim@yourlab.onmicrosoft.com from 185.220.101.45",
  "description": "Sentinel incident #<n> (learning lab). Link: <incidentUrl>",
  "severity": 3,
  "tags": ["sentinel-<n>", "learning-lab", "brute-force"],
  "sourceRef": "sentinel-<n>"
}

### 2. Add an observable to the case
POST {{thehive}}/api/v1/case/{{case.response.body._id}}/observable
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dataType": "ip", "data": "185.220.101.45", "message": "Attacker IP from Sentinel", "ioc": true }

### 3. Find closed lab cases (polling alternative to webhooks)
POST {{thehive}}/api/v1/query
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": [
    { "_name": "listCase" },
    { "_name": "filter", "_and": [ { "_field": "status", "_value": "Resolved" }, { "_field": "tags", "_value": "learning-lab" } ] },
    { "_name": "sort", "_fields": [ { "_updatedAt": "desc" } ] },
    { "_name": "page", "from": 0, "to": 20 }
  ]
}
